# The `caos-conversation-list` tool (SPEC, "Tools"): the std/go worker image
# with this directory's script curried onto it, plus the `help` the agent
# registers it by. The sibling of caos-conversation, which reads ONE conversation
# by the hash of its tip: this finds the hashes. Like it, it touches no source
# tree, so it needs no `@in`.
#
# The docs are a HERE-STRING, so they live in the `.caos-expr` — which is
# STRIPPED from the tree the expression is evaluated against. Editing them
# re-keys this tool's arg tree and nothing else: no build sees these bytes.
HELP=<<END
List the conversations recorded on this caos server — for example Claude Code sessions
that `caos mcp hook` recorded — NEWEST FIRST, one per line: the UTC time of the last
message, the conversation id, the hash of its current tip commit, its title, and who has
it (`user:active` or `user:archived`). `limit=N` is therefore the N most recent. Pass a
tip hash to `caos-conversation` to read one.

Conversations live as git refs on the server: `refs/caos/v3/conversations/<hex id>/head`
is the tip, and `refs/caos/v3/users/<hex user>/conversations/{active,archived}/<hex id>`
records who has it. This reads those refs; nothing is cloned. A Claude Code session's id
is `cc/<session-id>`.

THE TIME is the committer time of the tip commit: refs carry none, so every tip is read
to sort, which costs one fetch per conversation. A conversation whose tip cannot be read
is listed last with the reason. Use `filter` (a substring of the id or title) to narrow it.
@param [filter] Keep only conversations whose id or title contains this text (case-insensitive).
@param [limit] Print at most this many conversations (default 50; 0 for all).
@param [titles] Set to 0 to skip reading each tip's title, which costs one fetch per conversation (default 1).
END
curry --base:@=DEEP-DEPS/go --worker1:@=worker.go --help=$HELP
